# Rules
The rules specification is a game contract that defines turns, scores and session changes in Neon Pairs.

Status: spec version 2.2.

A turn reveals two eligible cards. A match adds one pair, while a miss gives you time to remember the faces before both cards turn back.

## Board

- R01 - Support square boards with side lengths `4`, `6`, `8`, `10`, `12`, `14` and `16`. Every face occurs exactly twice. Positions run from zero in row order.

The deal comes from the board code defined in [Reproducibility](reproducibility.md).

## Turn

- R02 - The first valid card activation reveals that card. Activating it again or activating a matched card has no game effect.
- R03 - The next valid activation reveals a different unmatched card. If the two faces match, keep them revealed and add one matched pair immediately.
- R04 - If the faces differ, show both for `800` active milliseconds, then close both together. Ignore all card activation during this interval. Pause the interval while the page is hidden or an imported snapshot awaits Resume.
- R05 - Add one move when the second valid card is revealed. The first reveal and ignored activation add no moves. Matches and misses each cost one move until the count reaches `999999`. At that cap the count stops increasing. Play continues normally, pairs still match and the game still completes. Show the current move count throughout play as `Moves: N`.

For example, revealing two matching cards produces one move and one matched pair. Revealing the same first card twice still leaves one revealed card and zero moves.

## Completion

- R06 - Give one point per matched pair and no other score. Show matched pairs against the board's total pairs throughout play as `Pairs: M/T`, where `M` is matched pairs and `T` is the total. Complete the game when every pair is matched. Show the final moves and elapsed time with a completion banner. Apply the completion motion defined in [Visuals](visuals.md).


## Clock

- R07 - Start elapsed time on the first valid reveal. Count active milliseconds while the page is shown. Pause while the page is hidden or an imported snapshot awaits Resume. Stop at completion. Rendering frequency doesn't change the elapsed time. Cap elapsed time at `359999999` milliseconds. At the cap, play continues normally and the clock shows the capped time.

Show the clock throughout play as `Time: m:ss`. Round elapsed seconds down, pad seconds to two digits and let minutes continue past 59. For example, 3600000ms shows `Time: 60:00`.

The mismatch interval and elapsed clock use the same active time. Showing the page again continues the interval from its remaining time.

## Session

- R08 - Start with `4` rows and `4` columns unless a saved supported size exists. Remember the last chosen size after reload. A page load starts a fresh deal. Loading a valid board code or snapshot also saves its size as the last chosen size. A failed load keeps the saved size unchanged.
- R09 - New Game creates a fresh seed at the current size. Restart keeps the current board code. Choosing a different size creates a fresh seed at that size. Each action clears the selection, matched pairs, moves and elapsed time.
- R10 - When play completes a game, keep its moves if they beat the saved best for that size. Keep these records after reload. An equal or worse result keeps the existing best. Starting or restarting a game keeps these records. Show the current size's best move count throughout play and after completion as `Best: N`. Before that size has a record, show `Best: none`.
- R11 - Invalid board codes and snapshots show an error and keep the current game. Invalid saved preferences are ignored. If storage is unavailable, play continues without saving.
- R12 - Starting, restarting, replacing or leaving a game invalidates its pending timer updates. An update from an earlier game or turn can't change the current game.

For example, restarting during a mismatch produces the original hidden deal with zero moves. The earlier mismatch timer can't close a card revealed in the restarted game.

Control behavior is defined in [Input](input.md). Return to [Neon Pairs](README.md) for the full specification.
# Technology
Technology is the build and language specification for Neon Pairs.

Status: spec version 2.2.

The game runs offline from one HTML file. Browser controls and inline SVG provide the board, input and artwork.

## Stack

- T01 - Use React with TypeScript and DOM rendering. Use native buttons, a native select and CSS Grid. Use no component library.

- T02 - Pin these packages and keep the lockfile. The stable versions were checked on 31 October 2026:

| Package | Version | Job |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `react`, `react-dom` | `19.3.1` | Browser UI |
| `typescript` | `7.0.2` | Type checking |
| `@types/react`, `@types/react-dom` | `19.3.0` | React types |
| `vite` | `8.3.5` | Build |
| `@vitejs/plugin-react` | `6.1.2` | React build integration |
| `vite-plugin-singlefile` | `2.3.4` | One HTML distribution |
| `vitest` | `5.0.5` | Unit tests |
| `@playwright/test` | `1.64.1` | Browser tests |
| `@types/node` | `24.19.2` | Build and test types |

TypeScript 7 is a stable release, as the [release announcement](https://devblogs.microsoft.com/typescript/announcing-typescript-7-0/) describes. The [React versions page](https://react.dev/versions) lists the stable React release family.

## Language

- T03 - Use Node.js 24.19 or later and npm. Keep browser and Node compiler projects separate. Use ESM, static imports and type-only imports for types.

Use Node `26.12.1`, npm `11.20.0` and Playwright `1.64.1` with Chromium `156.0.8078.4` as the named compatibility combination. Record the locked install, build, unit tests and browser journeys with those exact versions in the project README before calling the combination tested. Other supported versions need their own results.

- T04 - Enable TypeScript strictness, `noUncheckedIndexedAccess`, `exactOptionalPropertyTypes`, `verbatimModuleSyntax` and `erasableSyntaxOnly`. Keep type checking separate from bundling. Vite's [TypeScript support](https://vite.dev/guide/features.html#typescript) transpiles code without checking types.

- T05 - Model project data with exact types and validate unknown data where it enters the game. Use narrowing instead of `any`, suppressed diagnostics or unchecked casts. Derive state unions from their named values.

- T06 - Keep behavior and its code, styles and tests together. Aim for 100 lines per TypeScript file and keep authored TypeScript files at or below 200 lines. Split by behavior when a file grows. Use direct imports from the file that defines a behavior.

## Commands

- T07 - Provide these commands:

| Command | Result |
| --- | --- |
| `npm ci` | Install the locked dependencies |
| `npm run dev` | Serve the game locally |
| `npm run typecheck` | Check every compiler project |
| `npm test` | Run unit tests for the game rules |
| `npm run test:e2e` | Build from current source, then run browser checks in fresh contexts against that build |
| `npm run build` | Type check and emit `dist/index.html` |
| `npm run --silent replay -- PATH` | Read replay JSON with the output and exit behavior in C14 |

The browser command must fail if its build fails. It must never fall back to an earlier `dist`. Stop development servers and watchers you start before finishing the work.

## Distribution

- T08 - `dist/index.html` contains the script, styles and artwork needed for play. It opens directly from disk without another file or a network request. Use the system font. Keep browser zoom enabled.

- T09 - Serve the game from a local HTTP origin when checking saved preferences. Storage on a `file:` URL differs between browsers, as the [localStorage documentation](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Window/localStorage) explains. If storage is unavailable, play continues for the current session.

- T10 - Keep dependencies in development and build tooling where possible. The game uses no service, account, external asset, analytics or API key. Dependency installation can use the network. Playing the distribution doesn't use it.

The [game specification](README.md) connects this stack to the other requirements.
import { generateBoard } from './deck.ts';
import { SelectionKind } from './selection.ts';
import type { Board } from './deck.ts';
import type { Selection } from './selection.ts';

export const ELAPSED_MAX_MS = 359_999_999;
export const MISMATCH_MS = 800;
export const MOVES_MAX = 999_999;

export interface GameState extends Board {
  readonly matched: readonly number[];
  readonly selection: Selection;
  readonly moves: number;
  readonly elapsedMs: number;
  readonly started: boolean;
}

export function createGame(boardCode: string): GameState {
  return {
    ...generateBoard(boardCode),
    matched: [],
    selection: { kind: SelectionKind.closed },
    moves: 0,
    elapsedMs: 0,
    started: false,
  };
}

export function isWon(state: GameState): boolean {
  return state.matched.length === state.deck.length;
}

// The board reads one set per game state instead of searching the matched list for every card.
export function faceUpCards(state: Pick<GameState, 'matched' | 'selection'>): ReadonlySet<number> {
  const cards = new Set(state.matched);
  const selection = state.selection;
  if (selection.kind === SelectionKind.one) cards.add(selection.index);
  if (selection.kind === SelectionKind.mismatch) {
    cards.add(selection.first);
    cards.add(selection.second);
  }
  return cards;
}

export function activateCard(state: GameState, index: number): GameState {
  if (!Number.isInteger(index) || index < 0 || index >= state.deck.length) return state;
  if (state.matched.includes(index)) return state;
  switch (state.selection.kind) {
    case SelectionKind.closed:
      return { ...state, started: true, selection: { kind: SelectionKind.one, index } };
    case SelectionKind.one: {
      const first = state.selection.index;
      if (first === index) return state;
      const moves = Math.min(MOVES_MAX, state.moves + 1);
      if (state.deck[first] === state.deck[index]) {
        return {
          ...state,
          moves,
          matched: [...state.matched, first, index],
          selection: { kind: SelectionKind.closed },
        };
      }
      return {
        ...state,
        moves,
        selection: { kind: SelectionKind.mismatch, first, second: index, remainingMs: MISMATCH_MS },
      };
    }
    case SelectionKind.mismatch:
      return state;
    default:
      return unreachable(state.selection);
  }
}

export function advanceGame(state: GameState, milliseconds: number): GameState {
  if (!Number.isFinite(milliseconds) || milliseconds <= 0) return state;
  if (!state.started || isWon(state)) return state;
  const elapsedMs = Math.min(ELAPSED_MAX_MS, state.elapsedMs + milliseconds);
  if (state.selection.kind !== SelectionKind.mismatch) return { ...state, elapsedMs };
  const remainingMs = state.selection.remainingMs - milliseconds;
  const selection =
    remainingMs > 0 ? { ...state.selection, remainingMs } : { kind: SelectionKind.closed };
  return { ...state, elapsedMs, selection };
}

function unreachable(value: never): never {
  throw new Error(`Unknown selection: ${String(value)}`);
}
import { createGame, MOVES_MAX, ELAPSED_MAX_MS } from './game.ts';
import { parseBoardCode } from './deck.ts';
import {
  isJsonObject,
  isNonnegativeSafeInteger,
  isWithinBytes,
  parseJson,
} from './saved-format.ts';
import { readMatched, readSelection } from './snapshot-selection.ts';
import { SelectionKind } from './selection.ts';
import type { GameState } from './game.ts';

export const SNAPSHOT_VERSION = 1;
export const SNAPSHOT_MAX_BYTES = 65_536;
export const SNAPSHOT_KEYS = [
  'version',
  'boardCode',
  'matched',
  'selection',
  'moves',
  'elapsedMs',
  'started',
] as const;

export function encodeSnapshot(state: GameState): string {
  return JSON.stringify(
    {
      version: SNAPSHOT_VERSION,
      boardCode: state.boardCode,
      matched: [...state.matched].sort((left, right) => left - right),
      // Active time keeps its fractions in play. Export writes whole milliseconds, and rounding
      // pending time up keeps a mismatch at 1ms or more.
      selection:
        state.selection.kind === SelectionKind.mismatch
          ? { ...state.selection, remainingMs: Math.ceil(state.selection.remainingMs) }
          : state.selection,
      moves: state.moves,
      elapsedMs: Math.floor(state.elapsedMs),
      started: state.started,
    },
    null,
    2,
  );
}

export function decodeSnapshot(text: string): GameState | null {
  const value = isWithinBytes(text, SNAPSHOT_MAX_BYTES) ? parseJson(text) : undefined;
  if (
    !isJsonObject(value) ||
    !Object.keys(value).every((key, index) =>
      index === 0 ? key === SNAPSHOT_KEYS[0] : SNAPSHOT_KEYS.some((field) => field === key),
    ) ||
    Object.keys(value).length !== SNAPSHOT_KEYS.length ||
    value.version !== SNAPSHOT_VERSION
  )
    return null;
  if (typeof value.boardCode !== 'string' || !parseBoardCode(value.boardCode)) return null;
  if (
    !isNonnegativeSafeInteger(value.moves) ||
    value.moves > MOVES_MAX ||
    !isNonnegativeSafeInteger(value.elapsedMs) ||
    value.elapsedMs > ELAPSED_MAX_MS ||
    typeof value.started !== 'boolean'
  )
    return null;
  const initial = createGame(value.boardCode);
  const matched = readMatched(value.matched, initial);
  if (!matched) return null;
  const selection = readSelection(value.selection, initial, matched);
  if (!selection) return null;
  const state: GameState = {
    ...initial,
    matched,
    selection,
    moves: value.moves,
    elapsedMs: value.elapsedMs,
    started: value.started,
  };
  const minimumMoves = matched.length / 2 + (selection.kind === SelectionKind.mismatch ? 1 : 0);
  if (state.moves < minimumMoves) return null;
  if (
    !state.started &&
    (state.moves !== 0 ||
      state.elapsedMs !== 0 ||
      matched.length !== 0 ||
      selection.kind !== SelectionKind.closed)
  )
    return null;
  if (state.started && state.moves === 0 && selection.kind === SelectionKind.closed) return null;
  return state;
}
export function isJsonObject(value: unknown): value is Record<string, unknown> {
  return typeof value === 'object' && value !== null && !Array.isArray(value);
}

export function isNonnegativeSafeInteger(value: unknown): value is number {
  return typeof value === 'number' && Number.isSafeInteger(value) && value >= 0;
}

export function hasExactKeys(value: Record<string, unknown>, keys: readonly string[]): boolean {
  return (
    Object.keys(value).length === keys.length && keys.every((key) => Object.hasOwn(value, key))
  );
}

export function isWithinBytes(text: string, maxBytes: number): boolean {
  return new TextEncoder().encode(text).byteLength <= maxBytes;
}

// No JSON text parses to undefined, so it marks malformed input.
export function parseJson(text: string): unknown {
  try {
    const value: unknown = JSON.parse(text);
    return value;
  } catch {
    return undefined;
  }
}
import { hasExactKeys, isJsonObject, isNonnegativeSafeInteger } from './saved-format.ts';
import { MISMATCH_MS } from './game.ts';
import { SelectionKind, type Selection } from './selection.ts';
import type { GameState } from './game.ts';

export function readSelection(
  value: unknown,
  state: GameState,
  matched: readonly number[],
): Selection | null {
  if (!isJsonObject(value)) return null;
  const available = (index: unknown): index is number =>
    isNonnegativeSafeInteger(index) && index < state.deck.length && !matched.includes(index);
  switch (value.kind) {
    case SelectionKind.closed:
      return hasExactKeys(value, ['kind']) ? { kind: SelectionKind.closed } : null;
    case SelectionKind.one:
      return hasExactKeys(value, ['kind', 'index']) && available(value.index)
        ? { kind: SelectionKind.one, index: value.index }
        : null;
    case SelectionKind.mismatch:
      if (!hasExactKeys(value, ['kind', 'first', 'second', 'remainingMs'])) return null;
      if (!available(value.first) || !available(value.second) || value.first === value.second)
        return null;
      if (state.deck[value.first] === state.deck[value.second]) return null;
      if (
        !isNonnegativeSafeInteger(value.remainingMs) ||
        value.remainingMs < 1 ||
        value.remainingMs > MISMATCH_MS
      )
        return null;
      return {
        kind: SelectionKind.mismatch,
        first: value.first,
        second: value.second,
        remainingMs: value.remainingMs,
      };
    default:
      return null;
  }
}

export function readMatched(value: unknown, state: GameState): readonly number[] | null {
  if (!Array.isArray(value)) return null;
  const matched: number[] = [];
  const counts = new Map<number, number>();
  for (const index of value) {
    if (!isNonnegativeSafeInteger(index) || index >= state.deck.length || matched.includes(index))
      return null;
    const face = state.deck[index];
    if (face === undefined) return null;
    matched.push(index);
    counts.set(face, (counts.get(face) ?? 0) + 1);
  }
  return [...counts.values()].every((count) => count === 2) ? matched : null;
}
import { parseBoardCode } from './deck.ts';
import { activateCard, advanceGame, createGame } from './game.ts';
import {
  hasExactKeys,
  isJsonObject,
  isNonnegativeSafeInteger,
  isWithinBytes,
  parseJson,
} from './saved-format.ts';
import type { GameState } from './game.ts';

export const REPLAY_VERSION = 1;
export const REPLAY_MAX_BYTES = 1_048_576;
export const REPLAY_MAX_ACTIONS = 10_000;
const REPLAY_KEYS = ['version', 'boardCode', 'actions', 'endMs'];
const ACTION_KEYS = ['atMs', 'index'];

export const ReplayProblem = {
  tooLarge: 'tooLarge',
  malformedJson: 'malformedJson',
  format: 'format',
  boardCode: 'boardCode',
  actions: 'actions',
  endTime: 'endTime',
  action: 'action',
  order: 'order',
  index: 'index',
} as const;
export type ReplayProblemKind = (typeof ReplayProblem)[keyof typeof ReplayProblem];
type ReplayResult =
  { readonly state: GameState } | { readonly problem: ReplayProblemKind; readonly action?: number };

export function readReplay(text: string): ReplayResult {
  if (!isWithinBytes(text, REPLAY_MAX_BYTES)) return { problem: ReplayProblem.tooLarge };
  const value = parseJson(text);
  if (value === undefined) return { problem: ReplayProblem.malformedJson };
  if (!isJsonObject(value) || !hasExactKeys(value, REPLAY_KEYS) || value.version !== REPLAY_VERSION)
    return { problem: ReplayProblem.format };
  if (typeof value.boardCode !== 'string' || !parseBoardCode(value.boardCode))
    return { problem: ReplayProblem.boardCode };
  if (!Array.isArray(value.actions) || value.actions.length > REPLAY_MAX_ACTIONS)
    return { problem: ReplayProblem.actions };
  if (!isNonnegativeSafeInteger(value.endMs)) return { problem: ReplayProblem.endTime };
  let state = createGame(value.boardCode);
  let previousTime = 0;
  for (const [position, action] of value.actions.entries()) {
    if (
      !isJsonObject(action) ||
      !hasExactKeys(action, ACTION_KEYS) ||
      !isNonnegativeSafeInteger(action.atMs) ||
      !isNonnegativeSafeInteger(action.index)
    )
      return { problem: ReplayProblem.action, action: position };
    if (action.atMs < previousTime || action.atMs > value.endMs)
      return { problem: ReplayProblem.order, action: position };
    if (action.index >= state.deck.length)
      return { problem: ReplayProblem.index, action: position };
    state = activateCard(advanceGame(state, action.atMs - previousTime), action.index);
    previousTime = action.atMs;
  }
  return { state: advanceGame(state, value.endMs - previousTime) };
}

export function replayGame(text: string): GameState | null {
  const result = readReplay(text);
  return 'state' in result ? result.state : null;
}

